"""
Properties of code points from the Unicode Character Database, version 17.0.0.

- It gives the general category, the script, and the orbits of simple case folding.
- An orbit is the code points that fold to the same one.
- Standard.Regex reads its Unicode classes and its case folding from here.
- A code point is an Index; one past U+10FFFF has no property.
- Categories and scripts come back as static text: nothing is allocated for them.

    let category: Span[Nat8, Static] := generalCategory(65);
    var ranges: Buffer[Index] := allocateEmpty();
    let known: Bool := appendProperty("Greek", &!ranges);
"""
pragma Targets(Names => "linux openbsd freebsd darwin wasm");
import Standard.Buffer (
    Buffer
);

module Standard.UnicodeProperties is
    """
    The general category of a code point as its two letters, such as Lu or
    Nd.  Cn for a code point that is not assigned and for one past
    U+10FFFF.
    No contract: a view into its argument, whose length depends on it.
    """
    function generalCategory(point: Index): Span[Nat8, Static];

    """
    The script of a code point as Scripts.txt names it, such as Latin or
    Greek.  Unknown for a code point Scripts.txt does not list.
    No contract: a view into its argument, whose length depends on it.
    """
    function scriptOf(point: Index): Span[Nat8, Static];

    """
    Appends to ranges every code point with the named property, as pairs
    of the first and the last code point of each run, sorted and not
    touching.  The names are those Go's regexp takes: a general category
    by its short or long name (L, Lu, Letter, Uppercase_Letter, digit,
    punct), LC for Lu, Ll and Lt, a script by its name (Latin, Old_Italic),
    Any, Assigned and ASCII; C holds the unassigned code points with Cc,
    Cf, Co and Cs.  A name is matched loosely, without regard to the case
    of ASCII letters and with spaces, underscores and hyphens left out.
    False, with nothing appended, for a name it does not know.
    No contract: the answer is a Bool, nothing cheaper holds.
    """
    generic [R: Region, G: Region]
    function appendProperty(name: Span[Nat8, R], ranges: &![Buffer[Index], G]): Bool;

    """
    The next code point of the simple case folding orbit of point: the
    code points whose simple folding is the same, taken in a circle in the
    order of their numbers, so that following it from any one visits all.
    point itself when no other code point folds with it.
    No contract: a number read from its argument; its type gives its range, and nothing cheaper holds.
    """
    function nextInFoldOrbit(point: Index): Index;

    """
    Appends, as a pair of a code point with itself, every other code point
    that folds together with a code point from low to high.  With it a
    class of code points, already in ranges, is made to match without
    regard to case.
    No contract: it changes its argument in place; the accessors of its type say what holds afterwards.
    """
    generic [G: Region]
    function appendFoldPartners(low: Index, high: Index, ranges: &![Buffer[Index], G]): Unit;
end module.
